anika: Quick sync: a customer on Vercel Edge hit bundle size limits. Our SDK ended up pulling `undici`. We need a tiny, pasteable FAQ entry that covers ESM/CJS interop, edge runtime safety, and TypeScript typing workarounds.

vijay: Short checklist: 1) never top-level import undici, 2) prefer injected fetch, 3) dynamic import undici as a last resort, 4) ship ESM + CJS with conditional exports, 5) provide minimal ambient types.

marco: Minimal runtime shim (paste-friendly):
```js
// fetch-provider.mjs / .cjs compatible pattern
export function makeFetch(override) {
  return async function fetcher(input, init) {
    if (override) return override(input, init);
    if (globalThis.fetch) return globalThis.fetch(input, init);
    try { const { fetch } = await import('undici'); return fetch(input, init); }
    catch (e) { throw new Error('No fetch available. Install `undici` or pass a fetch implementation to makeFetch().'); }
  }
}
```
This keeps undici out of edge bundles because the edge entrypoint doesn't reference it.

iris: package.json / publishing tips to paste:
```json
"exports": {
  ".": { "import": "./dist/index.mjs", "require": "./dist/index.cjs" },
  "./fetch-shim": { "import": "./dist/fetch-shim.mjs", "require": "./dist/fetch-shim.cjs" }
},
"optionalDependencies": { "undici": "^5.0.0" },
"types": "dist/index.d.ts"
```
- `fetch-shim` should be a tiny module that just does: `export default globalThis.fetch`. Bundlers for browsers/edges pick that path.

vijay: Types caveat: many Node TS projects don't include the DOM lib. Two pragmatic options to document: (A) ask consumers to add "DOM" to `tsconfig.lib`, or (B) ship tiny ambient types so downstream TS compiles without DOM. Example minimal type file to include in the package:
```ts
// types/minifetch.d.ts
export type FetchLike = (input: string | URL, init?: any) => Promise<any>;
export default FetchLike;
```
Then point `types` to your bundled d.ts or include under `exports` as needed. This avoids leaking Request/Response DOM types.

marco: CI test idea: on PRs run `npm pack` for the edge entrypoint and `tar -tf` the artifact to assert `undici` files are NOT included. Add Node 14/16/18 matrix tests and a lightweight Cloudflare Worker smoke test to ensure global fetch path works.

anika: What about CJS consumers? If they `require()` the package and call `makeFetch()` they need to await the returned fetcher sometimes. Add a one-line note in README: "CJS: the factory may async-load a fallback; await the fetcher before calling it."

ci-bot: Added job `edge-bundle-check` to run pack + tar inspection and fail when undici is present in edge artifacts.

iris: Extra troubleshooting FAQ blurb for README: "Still seeing undici? Check package-lock for optionalDependencies, check your bundler's resolve preferences (exports/browser), and search codebase for any top-level `import 'undici'` or `require('undici')`."

anika: Great, that's concise. I'll add a 3-line recipe box for README (Edge / Node18+ / Node14/16) and open a PR with the shim, types, package.json snippets, and CI job. Thanks all :thumbsup:
